  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0424\" is used to store information about users, systems, and their interactions. It consists of four tables: User, System, Login_record, and System_authorization.\nThe User table contains information about individual users, including their account status, email, last login time, login IP, password, phone number, user ID, and username. The User ID is the primary key, and the username is unique.\nThe System table contains information about systems, including their access time, approval required, callback URL, enabled status, secret key, system ID, system domain, system name, and token validity period. The system ID is the primary key.\nThe Login_record table contains information about user login records, including the expiration time, login IP, login time, logout time, system ID, token, user ID, validity, and primary key (user ID and system ID). The system ID and user ID are foreign keys that reference the System and User tables, respectively.\nThe System_authorization table contains information about system authorizations, including the authorization time, effective status, expiration time, system ID, user ID, and primary key (user ID and system ID). The system ID and user ID are foreign keys that reference the System and User tables, respectively.\nIn summary, the schema stores information about users, systems, and their interactions, with each table representing a different aspect of the data. The primary keys and foreign keys ensure referential integrity, while the unique constraints ensure entity integrity.",
  "gold_question": "This is a comprehensive system management platform. For user management, the system maintains basic user information including user ID, username, password, phone number, and email, while recording user status information including account status, last login time, and login IP. For system management, the platform maintains basic system information including system ID, system name, system domain, and access time, records system configuration information including callback URL, secret key, and token validity period, and manages system status including whether enabled and whether approval is required. For login records, the system maintains basic login information including user ID, system ID, login time, and login IP, records session information including token and expiration time, and manages login status including validity and logout time. For system authorization relationships, the platform maintains authorization information including user ID, system ID, and authorization time, and manages authorization status including whether effective and expiration time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0424.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0424\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `account_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_login_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `login_ip` varchar(45) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `system` (\n  `system_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `system_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `system_domain` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `secret_key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `callback_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `enabled_status` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `approval_required` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `access_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `token_validity_period` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`system_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `login_record` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `system_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `login_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `logout_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `login_ip` varchar(45) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `validity` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `system_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `login_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `login_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`system_id`) REFERENCES `system` (`system_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `system_authorization` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `system_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `authorization_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `effective_status` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `system_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `system_authorization_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `system_authorization_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`system_id`) REFERENCES `system` (`system_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
